## Full from-scratch test run

### Step 0 — point `.env` at the right DB, with the right dimension
Make sure your `.env` (on your laptop) has:
```
PG_DATABASE=Knowledgeops_gw_1536
AZURE_PG_DATABASE=Knowledgeops_gw_1536
EMBEDDING_DIMENSIONS=1536
```
This is the fix from earlier — without it, `step4` will fail again with the same `expected 1536 dimensions, not 3072` error. `Knowledgeops_gw_1536` already has the correct `vector(1536)` schema from your earlier `db/create_new_db.py` run, so we don't need to recreate it.

### Step 1 — wipe it to a true blank slate
Connect to `Knowledgeops_gw_1536` (via your pgAdmin/VS Code Postgres extension, same place you ran the count queries) and run:
```sql
TRUNCATE ticket_records, chat_rca_records, release_note_records, runbook_records,
         curation_audit_log, kb_refresh_log, ingestion_state, kb_units
RESTART IDENTITY;
```
This clears every row from all 4 source tables plus the governance/audit tables and `kb_units`, so nothing is left over from the earlier test run.

